---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro"
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy — Neden"
  description="How the Neden website and desktop player handle your data."
>
  <article class="site-container prose-page">
    <h1>Your videos stay yours.</h1>
    <p>
      Neden is an independent, open-source project. The website and the desktop
      player handle different kinds of information.
    </p>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      There are no advertising trackers or analytics scripts on this site.
      Cloudflare hosts the website and processes network information, including
      IP addresses, to deliver and protect it. See{" "}
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">
        Cloudflare’s privacy policy
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    {import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_URL && (
      <>
        <h2>Optional Neden accounts — test environment</h2>
        <p>
          Account sign-in uses Better Auth on Cloudflare. We store your name,
          email, password hash, verification status, and session records.
          Passwords are hashed before storage. A necessary session cookie keeps
          you signed in. Cloudflare sends verification and password recovery
          messages. Temporary rate-limit records help protect accounts from
          repeated sign-in attempts.
        </p>
        <p>
          Hosted AI and subscriptions are not open yet. The planned service
          sends selected subtitle text and conversation context to DeepSeek.
          Videos and local flashcards stay on your computer. Our service does
          not store prompt or response text; the AI provider has its own data
          handling practices. Usage records contain request identifiers,
          allowance counts, and token counts. Old usage records are pruned after
          100 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          Stripe handles payment details separately. Neden keeps a billing
          customer reference and subscription status. Deleting your account
          cancels any subscription and removes sign-in and usage records. A
          minimal deletion marker and billing event identifiers remain to
          prevent delayed billing updates from restoring access; Stripe retains
          its own billing records. You can delete your account from the account
          page.
        </p>
      </>
    )}
    <p>
      Download and source links take you to GitHub, which has its own{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
        privacy policy
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <h2>The desktop player</h2>
    <p>
      Playback history, settings, and saved flashcards are stored on your
      computer. API credentials are stored through the operating system’s
      credential service. You can clear playback history in the app’s settings.
    </p>
    <h2>AI features</h2>
    <p>
      When you ask for a definition, explanation, or follow-up, Neden sends the
      relevant text and subtitle context to the provider you configure. That
      provider’s data handling, retention, and billing rules apply. Video
      playback itself does not require an AI request.
    </p>
    <h2>Update checks and support</h2>
    <p>
      Versions with a manual update checker contact GitHub only when you choose
      to check for updates. GitHub receives normal connection information,
      including your IP address; the request contains no media or profile data.
      Copy diagnostics places selected technical details on your clipboard.
      Reports are sent only when you choose to submit them.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions and source</h2>
    <p>
      You can inspect the implementation or report a concern in the{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/HanifCarroll/Neden">Neden repository</a>.
      Please keep API keys, private filenames, and other personal information
      out of public reports.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
